cuDNN dlopens its engine sublibraries by soname. Every other engine is a link
dependency of `:cudnn`, so it is already in the link map when cuDNN asks for it;
`libcudnn_engines_tensor_ir` was not, so it had to be found on disk. It never
is: `libcudnn.so.9`'s RUNPATH is `$ORIGIN`, and bazel gives every cc_import its
own `_solib_*` directory holding one symlink, so `$ORIGIN` is a directory that
contains nothing else.

The result is that every block-scaled dot (the tensor_ir engines serve
CUDNN_TENSOR_REORDERING_F8_128x4) fails to build its graph with
CUDNN_STATUS_SUBLIBRARY_LOADING_FAILED, the autotuner drops cuDNN, and the
fusion silently falls back to Triton.

--- a/gpu/cuda/build_templates/cuda_cudnn.BUILD.tpl
+++ b/gpu/cuda/build_templates/cuda_cudnn.BUILD.tpl
@@ -55,6 +55,12 @@
 )

 cc_import(
+    name = "cudnn_engines_tensor_ir",
+    hdrs = [":headers"],
+    shared_library = "lib/libcudnn_engines_tensor_ir.so.%{libcudnn_version}",
+)
+
+cc_import(
     name = "cudnn_main",
     hdrs = [":headers"],
     shared_library = "lib/libcudnn.so.%{libcudnn_version}",
@@ -131,6 +137,7 @@
       %{comment}":cudnn_cnn",
       %{comment}":cudnn_adv",
       %{comment}":cudnn_engines_runtime_compiled",
+      %{comment}":cudnn_engines_tensor_ir",
       %{comment}":cudnn_heuristic",
       %{comment}":cudnn_main",
       %{comment}]) + ["@cuda_nvrtc//:nvrtc"],
